#! seed 1861
# Civil War Strategy as a game of two players (QB64Rust's tools/screen/README.md, "Places and rules").
# In the Utility menu: 2 Player. Each month the Union plays, then the screen is blanked for the Rebel player ("press
# a key"), who plays too. In the first Rebel turn: COMMANDS, Detach (the Rebels' own command) of the army at Front
# Royal, then Detach again, left. Then END TURN for both sides by rules: 47 main menus to the time limit, the end
# screen, a Hall of Fame name for each side, Game Over, Quit.

# The waits: a space each (1:T is the blank screen before a player's turn); a Retreat menu: the city it starts on; a
# main menu: END TURN; the End Turn and End Game menus: Yes; the Options at the end: Quit this Game.
rule 1:R key space
rule 1:T key space
rule 1:P key space
rule 1:B key space
rule 1:U key space
rule 1:K key space
rule 1:I key space
rule 1:N key space
rule 1:S key space
rule 1:H key space
rule 1:G key space
rule 1:F key space
rule 1:L key space
rule 2:M text e
rule 2:E text y
rule 2:R key enter
rule 2:O text q

# The title menu: Start NEW Game; March 1861, the Union's main menu: UTILITY, 2 Player, out.
play until 2:V
digest
text s
# The scenario menu: the Standard Map.
play until 2:S
text s
play until 2:M
digest
text u
prompt
text 1
prompt
digest
key esc
# The Union: END TURN, Yes.
prompt
text e
prompt
text y
# The Rebel turn (after the blank screen): COMMANDS, Detach from Front Royal; Detach again (the cursor is on it), Esc.
play until 2:M
digest
text c
prompt
text d
prompt
digest
key enter
prompt
digest
key enter
prompt
key esc
# Both sides' turns: the main menu, END TURN (and Yes by the rule).
repeat 47
play until 2:M
digest
text e
end
# March 1865: time expired; End Game (Yes by the rule), the Options: Quit.
play until 2:O
state
text q
# A name for each side's Hall of Fame; Game Over; the title menu: Quit; END's key.
play until 4
state
text Grant
key enter
play until 4
state
text Lee
key enter
play until 2:V
digest
text q
repeat space
